  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Six rounds of the granny construction reach 15 cm, the standard size for a single-motif cushion front — a useful target for colour planning before committing to a full blanket. Each round adds one new "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " per side, so by round 6 each side carries 4 clusters between the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chain-2-corner"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "chain-2 corners"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " closes the centre hole completely, which matters at this size because a loose centre gap reads clearly at 15 cm. Finish with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to square up the corners."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 55 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "15 × 15 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. Check at round 4: target 10 cm. If smaller or larger, adjust hook size before continuing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr) — UK: yarn over once before inserting hook"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl): 3 tr into same sp, join through all loops"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first tr throughout."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr into ring. Ch 2. *(3 tr into ring, ch 2); repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner ch-2 sp, ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in ch-1 sp on side. Ch 1. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner ch-2 sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. 3 tr in last ch-1 sp. Ch 1. Sl st to top of ch-3. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 8 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in each ch-1 sp across side, ch 1 between each. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * around. Sl st to top of ch-3. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 12 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 5"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in each ch-1 sp across side, ch 1 between each. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * around. Sl st to top of ch-3. (60 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 16 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 6"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in same corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in each ch-1 sp across side, ch 1 between each. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * around. Sl st to top of ch-3. Fasten off. (72 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 20 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 6
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in both ends using a tapestry needle. Wet-block: soak in cool water, squeeze gently, roll in a towel. Pin to 15 × 15 cm with blocking pins at each corner and along the sides. Leave until fully dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join using the slip-stitch join or the mattress stitch. For slip-stitch join: hold two squares right sides together, slip stitch through corresponding corner spaces and chain-1 spaces along each side. Work 1 sl st into each cluster top and 1 into each ch-1 sp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. Reshape while damp and dry flat. Re-block if corners curl after washing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Once round 6 is comfortable, the six-round granny square is the same construction for all larger versions — each additional round adds one cluster per side. Try making nine of these and joining them into a 45 × 45 cm cushion front, or work rounds 1 and 2 in a contrast colour and rounds 3 to 6 in the main colour for a clear two-colour result."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}